@* The guide for coordinators and position coaches: what each of the two can do, the first sign-in,
   then the work every coach does *@
<div class="wr-guide-cols">
    <div class="wr-guide-side">
        <div class="wr-guide-search" hidden data-guide-search-box>
            <svg class="wr-icon wr-icon-sm" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-search"></use></svg>
            <input type="search" class="form-control" placeholder="Search this guide" aria-label="Search the assistant coaches guide" autocomplete="off" data-guide-search />
        </div>
        <nav class="wr-guide-nav" aria-label="Assistant coaches guide">
            <p class="wr-guide-nav-title">Assistant coaches guide</p>
            <ul>
                <li><a href="#ac-glance">At a glance</a></li>
                <li><a href="#ac-start">Your first sign-in</a></li>
                <li><a href="#ac-depth">Depth chart</a></li>
                <li><a href="#ac-schedule">Schedule and attendance</a></li>
                <li><a href="#ac-playbook">Playbook</a></li>
                <li><a href="#ac-approvals">Your change requests</a></li>
                <li><a href="#ac-film">Game film</a></li>
                <li><a href="#ac-cutups">Cutups</a></li>
                <li><a href="#ac-tendencies">Tendencies</a></li>
                <li><a href="#ac-study">Study time</a></li>
                <li><a href="#ac-team">Roster and groups</a></li>
                <li><a href="#ac-questions">Common questions</a></li>
            </ul>
        </nav>
    </div>

    <div class="wr-guide-main">
        <p class="wr-guide-count" role="status" hidden data-guide-count></p>

        @* ---------- At a glance ---------- *@
        <section class="wr-guide-section" id="ac-glance">
            <header class="wr-guide-head">
                <span class="wr-guide-head-icon"><svg class="wr-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-staff"></use></svg></span>
                <div>
                    <h3>At a glance</h3>
                    <p>You coach part of the team. What you can change depends on your role and on the position groups the head coach gave you.</p>
                </div>
            </header>

            <div class="wr-guide-card">
                <h4>Coordinator or position coach?</h4>
                <div class="table-responsive">
                    <table class="table wr-guide-table wr-guide-compare">
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="col"><span class="visually-hidden">What</span></th>
                                <th scope="col">Coordinator</th>
                                <th scope="col">Position coach</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Your groups</th>
                                <td>Every group in your unit, plus any other group you are assigned to</td>
                                <td>The groups you are assigned to</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Set the order on the depth chart</th>
                                <td>At the positions of your groups</td>
                                <td>At the positions of your groups</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Start a new depth chart week</th>
                                <td>Yes</td>
                                <td>No</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Add and change schedule events</th>
                                <td>Yes</td>
                                <td>No, read only</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Take attendance</th>
                                <td>Yes</td>
                                <td>Yes</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Draw and change the playbook</th>
                                <td>Your unit's playbook, and those of your other groups' units</td>
                                <td>The playbooks of your groups' units</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Game film, cutups and tendencies</th>
                                <td>Yes, all of it</td>
                                <td>Yes, all of it</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Study time</th>
                                <td>The players of your groups</td>
                                <td>The players of your groups</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Groups, positions and a group's players</th>
                                <td>In your unit</td>
                                <td>No, read only</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Edit a player's roster details</th>
                                <td>Players of your unit</td>
                                <td>No, read only</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="wr-guide-glance">
                <div class="wr-guide-card">
                    <h4>Three things the head coach can change for you</h4>
                    <ul class="wr-guide-facts" role="list">
                        <li><b>Publish playbook changes without approval:</b> off unless the head coach switches it on. Until then your changes wait for approval.</li>
                        <li><b>Edit the depth chart:</b> on unless the head coach switches it off.</li>
                        <li><b>Record attendance:</b> on unless the head coach switches it off.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p class="wr-guide-small">Your dashboard shows all three under <b>Your permissions</b>.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="wr-guide-card">
                    <h4>Only the head coach can</h4>
                    <ul class="wr-guide-no" role="list">
                        <li><svg class="wr-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-minus"></use></svg>Add coaches and players, and reset passwords</li>
                        <li><svg class="wr-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-minus"></use></svg>Choose which coaches coach a group</li>
                        <li><svg class="wr-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-minus"></use></svg>Approve or reject playbook changes</li>
                        <li><svg class="wr-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-minus"></use></svg>Change the team's settings and delete a depth chart week</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        @* ---------- Your first sign-in ---------- *@
        <section class="wr-guide-section" id="ac-start">
            <header class="wr-guide-head">
                <span class="wr-guide-head-icon"><svg class="wr-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-key"></use></svg></span>
                <div>
                    <h3>Your first sign-in</h3>
                    <p>Your head coach makes your account. Two minutes and you are in.</p>
                </div>
            </header>

            <article class="wr-guide-task" id="ac-sign-in">
                <div class="wr-guide-task-head">
                    <h4>Sign in for the first time</h4>
                </div>
                <ol class="wr-guide-steps" role="list">
                    <li>Get your sign-in email and your temporary password from the head coach.</li>
                    <li>On the main page, choose <span class="wr-ui">Sign in</span> and enter them.</li>
                    <li>You are asked to choose your own password. Enter the temporary one as <b>Current password</b>, then a new one of at least 8 characters, twice.</li>
                    <li>Choose <span class="wr-ui">Change password</span>. You land on your dashboard.</li>
                </ol>
            </article>

            <article class="wr-guide-task" id="ac-check-role">
                <div class="wr-guide-task-head">
                    <h4>Check your role and your groups</h4>
                </div>
                <ul class="wr-guide-points" role="list">
                    <li>Your role and team are written under your name, at the bottom of the menu.</li>
                    <li>Your groups are in your row under Team <i aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</i> Coaching staff.</li>
                    <li>What the head coach lets you do is on your dashboard, under <b>Your permissions</b>.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="wr-guide-note">A group is missing? Only the head coach can add you to it.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="wr-guide-task" id="ac-menu">
                <div class="wr-guide-task-head">
                    <h4>Find your way around</h4>
                </div>
                <dl class="wr-guide-terms">
                    <div>
                        <dt>Dashboard</dt>
                        <dd>Your week on one page: the next event, this week's depth chart, playbook changes that are waiting, and the cutups.</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <dt>Game plan</dt>
                        <dd>Depth chart, Schedule, Playbook and Approvals.</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <dt>Film room</dt>
                        <dd>Game film, Cutups, Tendencies and Teams on film.</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <dt>Team</dt>
                        <dd>Roster, Coaching staff, Groups and positions, and Study time.</dd>
                    </div>
                </dl>
                <p class="wr-guide-note">On a phone, the menu opens from the button at the top left.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="wr-guide-task" id="ac-password">
                <div class="wr-guide-task-head">
                    <h4>Change or recover your password</h4>
                </div>
                <ul class="wr-guide-points" role="list">
                    <li><b>To change it:</b> click your name at the bottom of the menu and choose <span class="wr-ui">Change password</span>.</li>
                    <li><b>Forgot it?</b> Ask the head coach to reset it. You get a new temporary password and choose your own again at the next sign-in.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="wr-guide-note">A sign-in ends by itself after 30 minutes without activity. Just sign in again.</p>
            </article>
        </section>

        <partial name="_GuideCoachTasks" model='"ac"' />

        @* ---------- Roster and groups ---------- *@
        <section class="wr-guide-section" id="ac-team">
            <header class="wr-guide-head">
                <span class="wr-guide-head-icon"><svg class="wr-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-users"></use></svg></span>
                <div>
                    <h3>Roster and groups</h3>
                    <p>Who is on the team, who coaches whom, and the position groups everything else is built on.</p>
                </div>
            </header>

            <article class="wr-guide-task" id="ac-look-up">
                <div class="wr-guide-task-head">
                    <h4>Look someone up</h4>
                </div>
                <ul class="wr-guide-points" role="list">
                    <li><b>A player:</b> open Team <i aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</i> Roster and click the name. You see the roster details, the position groups and the player's coaches.</li>
                    <li><b>A coach:</b> open Team <i aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</i> Coaching staff for every coach's role, groups and email.</li>
                    <li><b>A group:</b> open Team <i aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</i> Groups and positions and click its name for its positions, coaches and players.</li>
                </ul>
            </article>

            <article class="wr-guide-task" id="ac-manage-groups">
                <div class="wr-guide-task-head">
                    <h4>Look after the groups of your unit</h4>
                    <span class="wr-guide-who">Coordinators</span>
                </div>
                <p class="wr-guide-where"><span class="visually-hidden">In the menu, under</span> Team <i aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</i> Groups and positions</p>
                <ol class="wr-guide-steps" role="list">
                    <li>To add a group, choose <span class="wr-ui">Add a group</span> beside your unit, type the <b>Name</b> and choose <span class="wr-ui">Create</span>.</li>
                    <li>Click a group's name to open it. <span class="wr-ui">Rename</span> changes its name.</li>
                    <li>Choose <b>Add a position</b> and give it a short <b>Code</b> for the depth chart, such as X or MLB, and a <b>Name</b>.</li>
                    <li>Choose <b>Change players</b>, tick everyone who belongs to the group and choose <span class="wr-ui">Save</span>.</li>
                </ol>
                <p class="wr-guide-note">
                    A player has to be in a position's group before they can go on its depth chart, and a player can be in several groups.
                    Which coaches coach a group is chosen by the head coach.
                </p>
                <p class="wr-guide-note wr-guide-warn">
                    A group is deleted only after its positions, and a position only when no depth chart lists a player there.
                    Each position code is used once per team.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="wr-guide-task" id="ac-edit-player">
                <div class="wr-guide-task-head">
                    <h4>Update a player's details or status</h4>
                    <span class="wr-guide-who">Coordinators</span>
                </div>
                <p class="wr-guide-where"><span class="visually-hidden">In the menu, under</span> Team <i aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</i> Roster</p>
                <ol class="wr-guide-steps" role="list">
                    <li>Choose <span class="wr-ui">Edit</span> at the end of the player's row.</li>
                    <li>Change the jersey number, grade, height or weight, or set the <b>Status</b> to Active, Injured or Inactive.</li>
                    <li>Choose <span class="wr-ui">Save</span>.</li>
                </ol>
                <p class="wr-guide-note">
                    This works for players in the groups of your unit. An injured player stays on the depth chart with an <b>Injured</b> badge;
                    an inactive player cannot be added to one.
                </p>
            </article>
        </section>

        @* ---------- Common questions ---------- *@
        <section class="wr-guide-section" id="ac-questions">
            <header class="wr-guide-head">
                <span class="wr-guide-head-icon"><svg class="wr-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-help"></use></svg></span>
                <div>
                    <h3>Common questions</h3>
                    <p>When something is missing or will not save, the reason is usually one of these.</p>
                </div>
            </header>

            <details class="wr-guide-faq">
                <summary>I do not see Edit on the depth chart.</summary>
                <p>
                    The position is outside your groups, or the head coach has switched off depth chart editing for your account.
                    Check your groups under Coaching staff and your permissions on your dashboard, then ask the head coach.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details class="wr-guide-faq">
                <summary>My new play has not reached the players.</summary>
                <p>
                    It is waiting for the head coach. Open Game plan, then Approvals: your change is on the <b>Waiting</b> tab until it is approved.
                    Players keep seeing the approved version in the meantime.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details class="wr-guide-faq">
                <summary>I cannot change a formation or a play.</summary>
                <p>
                    Either a change to it is already waiting for approval, or its playbook is outside the units you coach.
                    A waiting change of your own can be revised or withdrawn under Approvals.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details class="wr-guide-faq">
                <summary>I cannot record attendance.</summary>
                <p>
                    The reason is written at the top of the attendance sheet: tracking is switched off for the team, the head coach has switched it off
                    for your account, or the event has not come yet. Attendance opens on the day of the event.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details class="wr-guide-faq">
                <summary>A player says they cannot see my cutup.</summary>
                <p>
                    Open the cutup and read <b>Shared with</b>. A cutup shared with nobody is seen by coaches only. Choose <span class="wr-ui">Share</span>
                    and tick the team, the player's group or the player.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details class="wr-guide-faq">
                <summary>A play will not delete.</summary>
                <p>It is used in a cutup. Take it out of that cutup first, then delete it.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="wr-guide-faq">
                <summary>A player is missing from my study time list.</summary>
                <p>You see the players of the groups you coach. A player in none of your groups is not on your list.</p>
            </details>
        </section>

        <p class="wr-guide-empty" hidden data-guide-empty>Nothing in this guide matches. Try another word, such as "attendance" or "cutup".</p>
    </div>
</div>
